---
import ServicePage from '../../components/services/ServicePage.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const canonical = 'https://busqueneil.com/services/ai-automation-consultant';

const FAQ = [
  {
    q: 'Do you only advise, or do you build too?',
    a: "I build. The person asking the questions is the person building the fix, so nothing gets lost between a plan and the work. If you only want strategy slides, I'm not the right fit.",
  },
  {
    q: 'How do you find what to automate?',
    a: "You walk me through a normal week: where the hours go, what keeps breaking and what you'd hand off tomorrow if you could. I'll tell you what's worth handing to AI, what's better as a plain workflow, and what to leave alone.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you work on site?',
    a: "Most of the work is remote, wherever you are. I'm based in New Jersey, so I can meet in person in New Jersey or New York City when a kickoff or a working session is easier at the same table.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Can we start small?',
    a: 'Yes. Start with one build. If it pays off, we plan the next one or move to a monthly arrangement.',
  },
];
---
<ServicePage
  title="AI Automation Consultant in NJ and NYC | Neil Busque"
  description="Neil Busque finds the processes costing your team time, then builds the automation to fix them. Direct, hands-on consulting in NJ, NYC and remote."
  canonical={canonical}
  heading="An AI automation consultant who **builds the fix**."
  lead="Most teams don't need more software. They need someone to trace where the work gets stuck, decide what should change and build the fix."
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/services' },
    { name: 'AI Automation Consultant', url: canonical },
  ]}
  topic="AI automation consulting"
  artSeed="ai-automation-consultant"
  artPalette="paper"
  summary={{
    items: [
      "A map of where your team's hours go",
      'A short list of the jobs worth automating, in order',
      'The first automation built, not just planned',
      'Plain notes for your team, or ongoing help each month',
    ],
    facts: [
      { term: 'Good for', value: 'Teams that know something should change, but not what' },
      { term: 'How it starts', value: 'You walk me through a normal week for your team' },
      { term: 'What you own', value: 'Every workflow, document and account' },
    ],
  }}
  related={['meeting-notes-to-tasks', 'agency-os-assistant-asks-first']}
  relatedPalettes={['navy', 'paper']}
  faq={FAQ}
  service={{
    name: 'AI Automation Consultant',
    serviceType: ['AI automation consulting', 'Workflow automation', 'Business process automation', 'AI strategy'],
    areaServed: ['New Jersey', 'New York', 'New York City', 'United States', 'Remote'],
  }}
>
  <h2>What an AI automation consultant does</h2>
  <p>The work has two parts. First, trace the process closely enough to find the real bottleneck. Then build the fix and put it into the tools your team already uses. A strategy deck can be useful, but it doesn't run your follow-up on Tuesday morning.</p>
  <p>I handle both parts. The person asking the questions is also the person building the system.</p>

  <h2>When it is worth hiring one</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your team spends hours on work that needs no judgment.</li>
    <li>Leads or tickets go cold because follow-up depends on someone remembering.</li>
    <li>You pay for tools that don't talk to each other, so a person is the integration.</li>
    <li>You know something should be automated, but not what, or in what order.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you already know exactly what needs building, skip the consulting and tell me what to build.</p>

  <h2>Consultant, agency or in-house</h2>
  <p>An agency gives you a team and a repeatable process. An in-house hire gives you long-term ownership. A hands-on consultant makes sense when the problem is bounded, speed matters and you want a direct line to the builder. If your problem really needs a permanent owner, I'll say so on the first call.</p>

  <h2>How I run it</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>A first conversation.</strong> Where the hours go, what breaks and what you have already tried.</li>
    <li><strong>A clear scope and price.</strong> What gets automated, what doesn't and what done looks like.</li>
    <li><strong>The first build in days.</strong> You see it working on real data and tell me what to change.</li>
    <li><strong>Hand it over, or keep me on.</strong> It's your system either way.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What I build with</h2>
  <p>n8n, Zapier and GoHighLevel for workflows, and Claude with MCP tools where the task needs judgment. I use plain automation wherever a rule would do, because a model where a rule belongs is how automation becomes expensive and unpredictable. More on <a href="/services/ai-automation-services">AI automation services</a> and <a href="/services/ai-agent-development">AI agent development</a>.</p>

  <h2>Serving New Jersey, NYC and remote</h2>
  <p>I'm Neil Busque, based in New Jersey. I work with teams across New Jersey and New York City and remotely across the United States, on US Eastern time. Most of the work happens remotely, wherever you are.</p>

  <h2>See how I work first</h2>
  <p>In 2026 I shipped more than 40 apps, AI agents and automations. Before that, I built more than 20 production n8n workflows across more than 10 client accounts at a marketing agency, including one-click client onboarding that cut a 30-day process to 7. See <a href="/work">the work</a> and read <a href="/resources">the guides</a>.</p>
</ServicePage>
